    {
      "id": "1572162327682490509",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-17T08:11:48.283+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "1. If it's in the foundry cells the chip won't be broken because it tripped a DRC rule in your commercial DRC engine.\n2. Sounds like the open PDK contains geometry that's not particularly functional electrically where Calibre gets angry about it which would be appropriate if the structures would be electrically active.\n3. Technically yes, if you order default COB, but almost all the PAD rules are just advisory/bond-house-originated. The seal ring seems to not hit the special treatment for your DRC engine.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
